    "slug": "ecommerce-brands",
    "h1": "PR for Ecommerce Brands",
    "title": "PR for Ecommerce Brands | Digital Networking Agency",
    "description": "Press coverage for ecommerce and DTC brands — building trust that lowers acquisition cost, and how the process works.",
    "body": "<p>A shopper sees your ad, gets interested, and searches your brand name before entering a card. That search is where the sale is won or lost.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-press-works-for-dtc-brands\">Why press works for DTC brands</h2>\n<p>Paid acquisition has one weakness: it brings people who do not know you to a page asking for money.</p>\n<p>The gap between click and purchase is trust. A published feature fills it — when a shopper searches your brand and finds real coverage, the \"is this legitimate?\" question resolves quietly. That shows up as conversion rate, which shows up as lower acquisition cost.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-most-brands-get-wrong\">What most brands get wrong</h2>\n<p>They pitch the product launch.</p>\n<p>Editors receive hundreds of those. What they publish is the story behind it: why you built it, what was broken in your category, the supply chain problem you solved, the thing customers kept telling you that nobody was acting on.</p>\n<p>The product is the payoff, not the pitch.</p>\n<h2 id=\"where-we-place-ecommerce-clients\">Where we place ecommerce clients</h2>\n<p>Lifestyle, business and consumer publications — including Women's Journal, MSN, NY Weekly, CEO Weekly and LA Wire.</p>\n<p>We match the outlet to your customer. A wellness brand and a B2B supplier need different rooms.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-a-feature-does-for-your-business\">What a feature does for your business</h2>\n<p>A permanent, indexed article that appears when a shopper searches your brand. An \"as seen in\" asset for your site and packaging. Something that makes retail and wholesale conversations easier, and that supports a higher price point.</p>\n<p>For brands raising, it is also the fastest way to look established.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-it-works\">How it works</h2>\n<p>Share your story and your customer. We develop the angle, write the piece to editorial standard, and manage placement. You review and revise until it is right, and nothing publishes without your approval.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Will press drive sales directly?</h3>\n<p>Occasionally, but that is not the main mechanism. The reliable effect is on conversion — traffic you already paid for closes better when the brand search backs you up.</p>\n<h3>We are a small brand. Is it worth it?</h3>\n<p>Small brands benefit most, because the credibility gap is widest. An established brand already has coverage; you are buying the thing they already have.</p>\n<h3>Can we use it on our site and packaging?</h3>\n<p>Yes — that is one of the highest-value uses. Describe accurately what it is, and link to the live article wherever you can.</p>",
