    "slug": "models",
    "h1": "PR for Models",
    "title": "PR for Models: PR Agency for Models | DNA PR",
    "description": "PR for models: what a PR agency for models does, the stories fashion editors want, where we place features and how press builds a career beyond the portfolio.",
    "body": "<p>A PR agency for models gets you written about in the fashion, lifestyle and culture publications that casting directors, brands, photographers and agencies read, so that a search for your name shows features and interviews rather than only a portfolio and a social feed. It turns a face people recognise into a person they know something about.</p>\n<p>This page explains how PR for models works, which stories land, where we place models and how to choose the right agency.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-press-works-for-models\">Why press works for models</h2>\n<p>Modelling is visual, but careers are built on more than images. Brands choosing a face for a campaign want to know who that person is, what they stand for and how they will come across in an interview. A portfolio cannot tell them.</p>\n<p>Press can. A profile in a credible title shows your personality, your background and your interests. It gives a casting director a reason to remember you, and a brand a reason to feel confident putting you in front of its customers.</p>\n<p>It also helps with the long game. Many models move into acting, presenting, design, wellness or their own brands. A record of coverage makes that move far easier, because the public already knows you as more than a picture.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-a-pr-agency-for-models-does\">What a PR agency for models does</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Finds the story.</strong> Your route into modelling, your heritage, your work behind the camera, your advocacy, your business.</li><li><strong>Writes it to the publication's standard.</strong> Features and interviews that read like the fashion or lifestyle title they appear in.</li><li><strong>Places it.</strong> Matching the story to fashion, beauty, lifestyle and culture publications that fit your look and your goals.</li><li><strong>Times it.</strong> Lining coverage up with a major campaign, a fashion week, a cover shoot or a new venture.</li><li><strong>Works with your agency.</strong> Coordinating with your mother agency or management, so coverage supports bookings rather than clashing with them.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-stories-that-work-for-models\">The stories that work for models</h2>\n<p>Fashion editors see beautiful pictures every day. What they look for is a story. Angles that tend to work:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>The route in.</strong> Being scouted somewhere unexpected, a late start or a switch from another career.</li><li><strong>The person behind the image.</strong> Interests, studies, family and culture.</li><li><strong>The advocacy.</strong> Body diversity, sustainability, mental health or representation, told with depth rather than slogans.</li><li><strong>The business.</strong> A clothing line, a beauty brand or a creative studio.</li><li><strong>The industry view.</strong> What modelling is really like now, from someone inside it.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"where-we-place-models\">Where we place models</h2>\n<p>We work across fashion, lifestyle and culture publications, including <a href=\"/get-featured-in/flaunt\">Flaunt</a>, <a href=\"/get-featured-in/galore-magazine\">Galore Magazine</a>, <a href=\"/get-featured-in/maxim\">Maxim</a>, <a href=\"/get-featured-in/glamour\">Glamour</a>, <a href=\"/get-featured-in/elle-uk\">Elle UK</a>, <a href=\"/get-featured-in/harpers-bazaar-australia\">Harper's Bazaar Australia</a> and <a href=\"/get-featured-in/ny-weekly\">NY Weekly</a>.</p>\n<p>The right title depends on your market and your direction. An editorial model, a commercial model and a fitness model need different rooms. For the most selective names, each publication page explains honestly how coverage happens there and what is realistic, and we tell you where we are pitching and why before anything is written. You can browse every title on our pages about <a href=\"/get-featured-in\">where you can get featured</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-to-choose-a-pr-agency-for-models\">How to choose a PR agency for models</h2>\n<p>Ask every agency the same questions:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Which publications, specifically?</strong> Fashion titles vary hugely in tone and readership.</li><li><strong>Do you understand modelling?</strong> Ask how they would work alongside your agency's booking plans and exclusivity arrangements.</li><li><strong>Do I approve everything?</strong> The answer should be yes, every word, with your agency able to review too.</li><li><strong>What is the long-term plan?</strong> A single feature helps. A considered run of coverage builds a career.</li></ul>\n<p>Fashion coverage relies on strong images, so make sure the photographs you supply are ones you have permission to use, and check usage with photographers and your agency before anything is submitted.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-pr-for-models-costs\">What PR for models costs</h2>\n<p>It depends on the publications, how many features you need and over what period. A new face building a first profile needs something different from an established model launching a brand. We quote each model individually rather than selling a fixed package. For a full picture of how agencies charge, see <a href=\"/guides/how-much-does-a-pr-agency-cost\">how much a PR agency costs</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-it-works\">How it works</h2>\n<p>Share your story, your goals and where you want to be seen. We develop the angle, write the piece to the publication's standard and manage the placement. You review and revise until it is right, and nothing publishes without your approval. Coverage takes weeks rather than days, so plan it around the campaigns and seasons that matter to you.</p>\n<p>If you are moving into acting, our page on <a href=\"/pr-for/actors-and-filmmakers\">PR for actors and filmmakers</a> covers the next step, and our guide on <a href=\"/guides/how-to-build-a-personal-brand-with-press\">building a personal brand with press</a> explains how coverage compounds over a career.</p>\n<h2 id=\"frequently-asked-questions\">Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Do models need a PR agency?</h3>\n<p>Not always. Your modelling agency handles bookings. A PR agency adds something different: press coverage that tells your story, which helps when brands, casting directors and audiences search your name.</p>\n<h3>What does PR for models involve?</h3>\n<p>Finding the story behind your career, writing features and interviews to the standard of fashion and lifestyle publications, placing them, and timing coverage around campaigns, fashion weeks and new ventures.</p>\n<h3>Can PR help a model move into acting or business?</h3>\n<p>Yes. Coverage that shows your personality, interests and ambitions makes a career change more credible, because producers, partners and the public already know you as more than an image.</p>",
    "toc": [
      { "id": "why-press-works-for-models", "text": "Why press works for models" },
      { "id": "what-a-pr-agency-for-models-does", "text": "What a PR agency for models does" },
      { "id": "the-stories-that-work-for-models", "text": "The stories that work for models" },
      { "id": "where-we-place-models", "text": "Where we place models" },
      { "id": "how-to-choose-a-pr-agency-for-models", "text": "How to choose a PR agency for models" },
      { "id": "what-pr-for-models-costs", "text": "What PR for models costs" },
      { "id": "how-it-works", "text": "How it works" },
      { "id": "frequently-asked-questions", "text": "Frequently asked questions" }
    ],
    "takeaways": [
      "Brands and casting directors want to know the person, not only the portfolio.",
      "The best stories for models are about the route in, the advocacy and the business.",
      "A record of coverage makes a move into acting, presenting or a brand far easier."
    ]
